---
// Preview only: Local Services Ads page in Brandon's voice, on the shared King Kong frame.
import KkShell from '../../components/KkShell.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What are Local Services Ads?', a: "The ads at the very top of Google for local services, above the regular ads and above the map, with a Google Guaranteed or Google Screened badge next to your name. You pay per lead, not per click. People call or message you straight from the ad." },
  { q: "What's the difference between Google Guaranteed and Google Screened?", a: "Google Guaranteed is for home service trades. Google Screened is for professional services. Both mean Google checked you out. Which one you get depends on your category." },
  { q: 'Am I eligible?', a: "Depends on your trade and whether you can pass Google's checks: license, insurance, and background checks on the owner and the people in the field. Most home service and professional categories qualify. We'll tell you on the call." },
  { q: 'What does a lead cost?', a: "Benchmarks put the average home service lead around $50, most trades somewhere between $25 and $80. Roofing runs higher, HVAC and plumbing usually lower. Your city and your review count move it. The number that matters is cost per booked job, and we track that one." },
  { q: 'What if I get a junk lead?', a: "Google lets you dispute leads that aren't real jobs: wrong service, wrong area, spam. But only if somebody actually does it. We flag them so you get credited." },
  { q: 'Why does response time matter so much?', a: "Because Google ranks Local Services Ads partly on how fast you answer. Miss calls and reply slow and you drop down the list and pay more. Answer in five minutes and you climb. Same rule as everywhere else in our system." },
];
---

<KkShell
  title="Local Services Ads Agency (Preview)"
  description="Google Local Services Ads management, from the badge to the booked job, in the Dead River look."
  kicker="LOCAL SERVICES ADS"
  headline="THE VERY TOP OF GOOGLE, WITH A BADGE THAT SAYS YOU'RE CHECKED. AND YOU ONLY PAY WHEN THE PHONE RINGS."
  sub="Above the ads. Above the map. Pay per lead, not per click. Most businesses set it up wrong and lose the leads they already paid for."
  faqTitle="LOCAL SERVICES ADS, STRAIGHT ANSWERS"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="kk-dear">Hey,</p>
  <p>There's a spot on Google above everything else. Above the regular ads. Above the map. Three businesses, each with a badge that says Google checked them out.</p>
  <p>That's Local Services Ads, and here's the part most owners don't know. You don't pay per click up there. You pay per lead. Somebody calls or messages you through the ad, that's what you pay for. Nobody clicks around and leaves on your dime.</p>
  <p>So why isn't every business running them?</p>
  <h2>BECAUSE THEY GET STUCK, THEN THEY LEAK</h2>
  <p><strong>Stuck in verification.</strong> Background checks, license paperwork, insurance documents. Owners start the application, hit a wall, and the ads never go live. We've seen businesses sit "pending" for months.</p>
  <p><strong>Leads that go unanswered.</strong> This is the one that hurts. Google ranks you up there on how fast you respond. Miss the call, reply the next morning, and you drop down the list and the next lead costs more. You paid for a lead and then paid again for being slow.</p>
  <p><strong>Paying for junk.</strong> Wrong service, wrong area, spam. Google lets you dispute those and get credited. But somebody has to actually do it, every week, and nobody does.</p>
  <h2>WHAT WE DO</h2>
  <ul class="kk-list">
    <li><strong>Get you the badge.</strong> We walk you through the Google Guaranteed or Google Screened checks and the paperwork so the ads go live instead of sitting pending.</li>
    <li><strong>Set the profile up to win.</strong> Service types, service areas, hours, photos, set up the way Local Services Ads rank, not the way the wizard leaves them.</li>
    <li><strong>Budget and bids.</strong> A weekly budget and bid settings aimed at the jobs you actually want more of. Not every lead is worth the same.</li>
    <li><strong>Answer every lead fast.</strong> Every lead gets a response inside five minutes, because speed is the ranking, and because a lead that waits already hired the other guy.</li>
    <li><strong>Reviews after every job.</strong> Reviews feed the ranking up there too. One text, one tap, every time.</li>
    <li><strong>Dispute the junk.</strong> We flag invalid leads so you get your money back on them.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>THE NUMBER THAT MATTERS</h2>
  <p>Cost per lead is the number Google shows you. It's not the number that matters. Cost per booked job is.</p>
  <p>So every Local Services lead lands in your CRM with the rest of them, gets the same five-minute call back, and gets tracked through to whether it booked and what it was worth. That's how you know whether to turn the budget up or down. Not from a hunch. From the number.</p>
  <p>Local Services Ads run inside Demand Flow next to Google Ads, the list, and the map. Same phone, same follow-up, same guarantee.</p>
  <p class="kk-ps">P.S. If you've already got Local Services Ads running, bring the account to the call. The leads you're losing to slow replies and undisputed junk are usually the fastest money we find.</p>
</KkShell>
